WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670
A tiny seed can grow into a huge tree.

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.010
Its cell walls are made of cellulose,

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.360
and cellulose is built from glucose.

4
00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.690
That's a lot of carbon.

5
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.990
Yet a tree never eats a thing.

6
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.470
So where does all that
carbon come from?

7
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.050
In this mission, you'll
meet the word equation for

8
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:18.890
photosynthesis.

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.470
You'll see how chlorophyll,
inside chloroplasts,

10
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.250
absorbs the light
energy a plant needs.

11
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.210
And you'll follow the glucose
a plant makes as it becomes

12
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.210
starch, cellulose, and
fuel for respiration.

13
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.270
Your mission: find out where
a tree gets its carbon.
